# Generated by Jekyll? No - keep .nojekyll
#
# GitHub Pages runs Jekyll by default, and Jekyll ignores directories whose
# names begin with an underscore (including Next.js's /_next asset folder).
# The presence of this file disables Jekyll processing entirely.
#
# It is committed to /public so it is copied verbatim into the exported /out
# directory during `next build`. The GitHub Actions workflow also creates one
# defensively at deploy time.
